        "created_at": "2016-02-04T14:14:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>When you're \"opening your presents\" from Santa Guise, do you \"unwrap\" them all at once and then decide the order of which you want them to enter play, or do you flip them one at a time (either in the order they were put there or the order of your choice)? I'm guessing it's the first one because there's nothing to say they have to be done in a certain order and therefore falls under the \"simultaneous actions\" rule wherein players can decide.</p>",
